<section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="fast">
  <h2 id="fast">Reads the file table, not the folders</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    riptide opens the raw volume and reads the NTFS Master File Table in one sequential pass. It
    never walks the folder tree.
  </p>

  <div class="facts">
    <div class="panel fact">
      <span class="caps">First read</span>
      <span class="mono figure">4.87M records in 26 s</span>
      <span class="dim">On the author's machine.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="panel fact">
      <span class="caps">Rescan</span>
      <span class="mono figure">Under 1 s</span>
      <span class="dim">After the first read. Updates come from the NTFS change journal.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="panel fact">
      <span class="caps">Without admin rights</span>
      <span class="mono figure">Directory walk</span>
      <span class="dim">Slower, same results. riptide says which one ran.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }

  .fact {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    padding: var(--s-5);
  }

  .figure {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .fact .dim {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .facts {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
